Nitrocid changes
================

Released October 8th, 2026; version 0.2.1.0 (RC) (mod API 4.1.29.59); codename
Flaming Speed

This is a release candidate of the upcoming version of Nitrocid that is set to
release on November 5th, 2026. We have added several new features, including
an ability to more accurately search for a configuration key in the settings
textual user interface, a way to graphically manage users and groups, and an
ability to use POP mail that was removed in earlier versions of Nitrocid due
to an issue that caused Nitrocid to crash in ARM32 devices.

We have also updated calendar rendering and the whole kernel codebase, as well
as fixing some of the long standing bugs that were there in earlier versions.

We will populate the full changelogs once the release candidate version becomes
available, as we're working towards finalizing the official version.

FreeBSD support
---------------

We have finally added support for FreeBSD systems to Nitrocid the same way we
added support for Linux and macOS. Starting from this release, you can now
run Nitrocid more comfortably without any issues on FreeBSD systems. This
was realized by automated builds that are audited from time to time to make
sure that things run smoothly. We have tested this support on FreeBSD 15.0,
which means that if you are running this version of FreeBSD, you can
confidently run Nitrocid there.

SpecProbe, Magico, BassBoom, and Terminaux have all earned support for
FreeBSD after a successful experiment. This made our list of supported
operating systems for our projects bigger. FreeBSD support is determined by
our official support schedule as you can see in our main GitBook instance at
https://aptivi.gitbook.io/aptivi/csharp-libraries/support-periods.
